---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// TODO: fill in before publishing.
const company = 'Yantagram';
const effectiveDate = 'October 5, 2026';
---

<Layout>
	<div class="container privacy-page">
		<a href="/" class="home-link">&larr; Home</a>
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<div class="effective-date">
			<span class="label">Effective Date:</span>
			<span>{effectiveDate}</span>
		</div>
		<p>
			This Privacy Policy explains what information {company} ("Yantagram", "we", "us", or "our") handles when you use the Yantagram mobile
			application, the optional internet relay and push notification services, and this website (together, the "Services"). It should be read
			together with our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>In short:</strong> Yantagram is designed so that we know as little about you as possible. There are no accounts, and we do not ask
			for your name, phone number, or email. Your messages are end-to-end encrypted and stored only on your device. We do not use analytics,
			advertising, or tracking tools, and we do not sell or share your personal information.
		</p>

		<ul>
			<li>
				<h2>1. Information Stored Only on Your Device</h2>
				<p>
					The following information is created and stored on your device, in encrypted storage. We do not collect it and cannot access it:
				</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>your identity and encryption keys;</li>
					<li>your contacts, groups, and the display names you choose;</li>
					<li>your messages, images, and conversation history; and</li>
					<li>your settings and any in-app purchase status.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					This information is deleted when messages expire under your disappearing message settings, when you use the panic wipe, or when you
					uninstall the application. Because we never receive it, we cannot recover it for you.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>2. Device Permissions</h2>
				<p>The application asks for these permissions, and uses them only on your device:</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li><strong>Bluetooth</strong>, to discover and exchange encrypted messages with nearby devices.</li>
					<li><strong>Camera</strong>, to scan QR codes to add and verify contacts.</li>
					<li><strong>Photos</strong>, to let you choose images to send, or save images you receive.</li>
					<li><strong>Notifications</strong>, to alert you when new messages arrive.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>You can change these permissions at any time in your device settings, though some features may stop working.</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>3. Information Visible to Nearby Devices</h2>
				<p>
					To form the Bluetooth mesh, your device broadcasts signals that other nearby devices running Yantagram can detect, including a device
					identifier, and it forwards encrypted messages for other users. Nearby devices can observe that a Yantagram device is present and the
					timing and size of encrypted traffic, but they cannot read your messages. Any device can be operated by anyone, and we do not control
					what other users do with what their devices observe.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>4. Internet Relay</h2>
				<p>
					When the internet relay is enabled, the application sends encrypted messages through relay servers so they can reach contacts who are not
					nearby. You can turn the relay off in the application's settings. When it is on, the relay we operate receives:
				</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li><strong>Encrypted messages</strong>, which we cannot read;</li>
					<li><strong>Routing tags</strong>, random-looking values that change every day and are not linked to your identity; and</li>
					<li><strong>Your IP address and connection times</strong>, which are necessary to deliver network traffic and to prevent abuse.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Encrypted messages are set to expire and are deleted from the relay within 7 days. If you add third-party relays in the application's
					settings, those relays are operated by others under their own policies, and we are not responsible for how they handle data.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>5. Push Notifications</h2>
				<p>
					When the internet relay is enabled, the application registers with our push notification service so your device can be woken when a
					message arrives for it. The service stores your device's push token, its platform (iOS or Android), and the routing tags described above.
					It never receives your identity, contacts, or message contents. Your registration is deleted when you turn the relay off, or automatically
					if it is not refreshed for 14 days.
				</p>
				<p>
					Push notifications are delivered by Apple Push Notification service or Google Firebase Cloud Messaging, which process your push token
					under their own privacy policies. Notifications we send do not contain message contents.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>6. Purchases</h2>
				<p>
					Optional in-app purchases are processed by the Apple App Store or Google Play. We do not receive your name, payment details, or billing
					address. Purchases are verified on your device and are not linked to your Yantagram identity. Apple and Google handle purchase data under
					their own privacy policies.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>7. Communications With Us</h2>
				<p>
					If you email us, for example to request beta access or ask for support, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to include.
					We use it only to respond to you and to manage the beta, and we delete it when it is no longer needed for those purposes.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>8. This Website</h2>
				<p>
					This website does not use cookies, analytics, or tracking tools. It stores your light or dark theme preference in your browser's local
					storage. Our hosting provider processes your IP address and standard request information to deliver the website, and fonts are loaded from
					Google Fonts, which receives your IP address when your browser requests them.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>9. How We Use and Share Information</h2>
				<p>
					We use the limited information described above only to provide, operate, secure, and improve the Services, prevent abuse, respond to you,
					and comply with the law. We do not sell or "share" personal information as those terms are defined under California law, and we do not use
					it for advertising or profiling.
				</p>
				<p>We disclose information only:</p>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>to service providers that host or deliver the Services on our behalf, such as our cloud hosting provider and Apple and Google for push notifications;</li>
					<li>when we believe in good faith that disclosure is required by law, legal process, or a government request, or is necessary to protect the rights, safety, or property of users, the public, or us; and</li>
					<li>in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, in which case this Privacy Policy will continue to apply to the information transferred.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Because of how Yantagram is designed, we hold very little information to disclose, and we cannot provide message contents, contacts, or
					identities, because we do not have them.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
				<ul class="disc-list">
					<li>Encrypted messages on our relay: deleted within 7 days.</li>
					<li>Push registrations: deleted when you turn the relay off, or 14 days after they were last refreshed.</li>
					<li>IP addresses: processed to deliver traffic and enforce rate limits, and not kept longer than needed for those purposes, except where needed to investigate abuse or comply with the law.</li>
					<li>Emails: kept only as long as needed to respond to you or manage the beta.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>11. Security</h2>
				<p>
					Messages are end-to-end encrypted, and data on your device is stored in encrypted form. However, no method of transmission or storage is
					completely secure, and Yantagram's security has not been formally audited by an independent third party. We cannot guarantee the security
					of any information.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>12. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
				<p>
					Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of your personal information, to object
					to or restrict certain processing, and to withdraw consent. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.
				</p>
				<p>
					Because Yantagram has no accounts, most of your data is under your direct control: you can turn off the relay to delete your push
					registration, use the panic wipe, or uninstall the application to delete everything on your device. For other requests, contact us at
					dev@yantagram.com. Because we do not link the information we hold to an identity, we may be unable to locate information about you, and
					we may need to ask you for information to verify a request. You may also have the right to complain to your local data protection
					authority.
				</p>
				<p>
					Where the GDPR or similar laws apply, we process information on the basis of performing our contract with you (to deliver messages and
					notifications), our legitimate interests (to secure the Services and prevent abuse), and compliance with legal obligations.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>13. International Users</h2>
				<p>
					Our relay and push notification servers are located in the United States. If you use the Services from outside the United States, the
					limited information described in this policy will be transferred to and processed in the United States, where data protection laws may
					differ from those in your country.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>14. Children</h2>
				<p>
					The Services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 (or the
					higher minimum age that applies in your country). If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, contact us and we will
					delete it.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>15. Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version will always be posted on this page with its effective date. If we
					make material changes, we will make reasonable efforts to notify you, for example through the application or this website.
				</p>
			</li>

			<li>
				<h2>16. Contact</h2>
				<p>
					If you have any questions or requests about this Privacy Policy, contact us at
					<a href="mailto:dev@yantagram.com">dev@yantagram.com</a>.
				</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.privacy-page {
		max-width: 800px;
		padding-top: 80px;
		padding-bottom: 80px;
	}

	.home-link {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
		font-weight: 500;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	.home-link:hover {
		color: var(--color-text);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.effective-date {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.effective-date .label {
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-right: 0.25rem;
	}

	p {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	li h2 {
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	li p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	strong {
		color: var(--color-heading);
	}

	.disc-list {
		list-style: disc;
		padding-left: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.disc-list li {
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--color-primary);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	a:hover {
		opacity: 0.8;
	}
</style>
